{* A block of text the user is meant to take away: shown in full, selectable, with a copy button.

	A textarea rather than an input because the things that end up here are long — an absolute
	path into a macOS bundle runs well past any sensible field width, and an input shows one
	field-width of it with no hint there is more. A textarea wraps, so the whole command is visible
	without scrolling it horizontally.

	readonly, not disabled: a disabled control cannot be selected or copied, which is the only
	thing this exists for. Its rows come from the caller, since only the caller knows how long
	the content runs.

	The button sits *inside* the field, top right, rather than beside it: next to a textarea it
	stretched the row and left the two controls looking unrelated. Inside, it reads as part of
	the field it acts on, and the textarea keeps the dialog's full width. The padding that keeps
	the text clear of it is in settings.css.

	Icon only, with the label as its title and its accessible name: over a field the icon is
	unambiguous, and the word doubled what the field already says while eating the width the
	command needs. copy-field.js swaps both for "Copied" and raises the toast, which is what
	confirms the copy now that there is no label to change.

	The button is wired by src/Assets/javascript/copy-field.js, which binds every instance on the
	page by data attribute — no id to keep unique, and no inline handler, which the app's CSP
	would refuse anyway (strict-dynamic makes the 'unsafe-inline' beside it ignored).
*}
{parameters
	string $value,
	string $label,
	string $copy,
	string $copied,
	int $rows = 2
}
<div class="ad-copy" data-copy-field>
	<textarea class="ad-copy-value" readonly rows="{$rows}" aria-label="{$label}"
		data-copy-value>{$value}</textarea>
	{* Inline SVG rather than a sprite or a font: two rectangles, currentColor, no extra request
		and it follows the theme's text colour on both schemes. aria-hidden because the button's
		aria-label already says what it does. *}
	<button type="button" class="ad-copy-button" data-copy-button data-copied="{$copied}"
		title="{$copy}" aria-label="{$copy}">
		<svg class="ad-copy-icon" viewBox="0 0 16 16" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" aria-hidden="true">
			<rect x="5.5" y="5.5" width="9" height="9" rx="1.5"/>
			<path d="M10.5 3.5v-1a1 1 0 0 0-1-1h-7a1 1 0 0 0-1 1v7a1 1 0 0 0 1 1h1"/>
		</svg>
	</button>
</div>
